[h1]个人日志[/h1]
[quote]把角色已掌握的技能、配方、技能书和培训媒体记录在原版日记本中。角色死亡后，同一服务器账号的新角色找回实体日志并读完，即可继承其中的知识。[/quote]

[h1]原版风格[/h1]
[list]
[*]使用原版日记本、书写工具、右键菜单、阅读动作、动画和进度条，不添加新物品、配方或独立界面。
[*]书写或阅读被打断时会保存已完成页数；再次操作从未完成处继续。
[*]没有任何依赖，可直接加入现有存档。
[*]日志必须真实存在于世界中；不会在重生时自动恢复。
[*]多人游戏由服务端计算、校验并提交读写结果，客户端不提交技能、配方或媒体数据。
[/list]

[h1]记录内容与时间[/h1]
[list]
[*]已有技能：只恢复当前角色缺少的技能经验。
[*]已知配方：记录已学会的配方。
[*]已读技能书：记录原版阅读页数、阅读进度与实际经验加成状态，并遵守原版等级区间。
[*]已看培训媒体：仅记录带永久技能、经验或配方奖励的 CD/VHS；纯娱乐媒体不会写入。
[*]书写与阅读时间会按实际写入或恢复的内容计算。
[/list]

[h1]沙盒选项[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]记录已有技能[/b]：控制技能经验是否写入并恢复。
[*][b]记录已知配方[/b]：控制配方是否写入并恢复。
[*][b]记录已读技能书[/b]：控制技能书阅读进度和经验加成是否写入并恢复。
[*][b]记录已看培训媒体[/b]：默认开启，控制有效培训媒体是否写入并恢复。
[*][b]书写时间倍率[/b]：1.0 为原版阅读时长，数值越小越快。
[*][b]阅读时间倍率[/b]：1.0 为原版阅读时长，并受原版阅读速度特质影响。
[*][b]记忆恢复比例[/b]：50%–100%。技能经验按数值计算；其余记录按数量恢复。重复阅读不会累加。
[/list]

[h1]使用方法[/h1]
[olist]
[*]把原版日记本和笔或铅笔放进背包，右键日记本选择 写日志。
[*]首次写完后成为个人日志；有新内容时可继续写入，也可使用另一本日记保存独立记录。
[*]死亡后，同一服务器账号的新角色找回实体日志，选择原版阅读。
[*]完成后只恢复当前角色缺少的内容，不会降低已有进度；其他玩家只能像原版文字物品一样阅读。
[/olist]

[h1]兼容性[/h1]
支持 Project Zomboid Build 42.20、单人游戏、多人游戏和专用服务器。移除模组后日志仍是原版日记本；重新安装后可继续识别有效记录。

Workshop ID: 3788037313
Mod ID: LegacyJournal

[hr]
[h1]English[/h1]
[h1]Personal Journal[/h1]
[quote]Record skills, recipes, skill books, and training media in a vanilla diary. After death, a new character on the same server account can recover the physical journal, finish reading it, and inherit its knowledge.[/quote]

[h1]Faithful to Vanilla[/h1]
[list]
[*]Uses vanilla diaries, writing tools, context menus, reading actions, animations, and progress bars. It adds no new item, recipe, or separate interface.
[*]Interrupted writing and reading save completed pages; the next action continues from where it stopped.
[*]There are no dependencies, and the mod can be added to an existing save.
[*]The journal must physically remain in the world. Nothing is restored automatically on respawn.
[*]In multiplayer, the server calculates, validates, and commits writing and reading. Clients do not submit skill, recipe, or media data.
[/list]

[h1]What It Records and How Long It Takes[/h1]
[list]
[*]Existing skills: restores only the skill XP missing from the current character.
[*]Known recipes: records learned recipes.
[*]Read skill books: records vanilla pages read and reading progress plus the active XP bonus state within vanilla level ranges.
[*]Watched training media: records only CDs and VHS tapes with permanent skill, XP, or recipe rewards. Entertainment-only media is not written.
[*]Writing and reading time scale with the content actually recorded or restored.
[/list]

[h1]Sandbox Options[/h1]
[list]
[*][b]Record existing skills[/b]: controls skill XP recording and recovery.
[*][b]Record known recipes[/b]: controls recipe recording and recovery.
[*][b]Record read skill books[/b]: controls skill-book reading progress and active XP bonus-state recording and recovery.
[*][b]Record Watched Training Media[/b]: enabled by default; controls recording and recovery of qualifying training media.
[*][b]Writing time multiplier[/b]: 1.0 uses vanilla reading time; lower values are faster.
[*][b]Reading time multiplier[/b]: 1.0 uses vanilla reading time and still respects vanilla reading-speed traits.
[*][b]Memory recovery percentage[/b]: 50%–100%. Skill XP is numerical; other records recover by count. Repeated reading does not stack.
[/list]

[h1]How To Use[/h1]
[olist]
[*]Keep a vanilla diary and a pen or pencil in the inventory, then right-click the diary and choose [b]Write Journal[/b].
[*]After the first entry it becomes a personal journal. Write again after learning more, or use another diary for an independent record.
[*]After death, a new character on the same server account recovers the physical journal and chooses the vanilla [b]Read[/b] action.
[*]Completion restores only what the current character lacks and never lowers existing progress. Other players can only read it as a vanilla written item.
[/olist]

[h1]Compatibility[/h1]
Supports Project Zomboid Build 42.20, singleplayer, multiplayer, and dedicated servers. Removing the mod leaves a vanilla diary; reinstalling recognizes valid records again.

